  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under the Restatement (Third) of Agency Section 1.04(7), a power of attorney is a written authorization granting an agent (attorney-in-fact) authority to act on the principal''s behalf in specified transactions. Sullivan''s document granting Carter authority over banking, checks, and securities fits this definition.
Wrong (B): A revocable trust agreement creates a separate legal entity to hold and manage assets, transferring ownership to the trust rather than authorizing an agent to act directly.
