-- Q11168: Agency and Regulation [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under UCC Section 2-601 (the perfect tender rule), the buyer may reject the entire shipment, accept the entire shipment, or accept some commercial units and reject the rest if the goods fail to conform to the contract in any respect. Even 12 undersized bolts out of 1,000 justify full rejection.
Wrong (A): The perfect tender rule does not include a materiality threshold. Any nonconformity, however minor, entitles the buyer to reject the entire shipment.
Wrong (C): While partial acceptance is permitted under Section 2-601, it is optional. The buyer is not required to accept conforming goods and reject only defective ones.
Wrong (D): The UCC does not require the buyer to negotiate a price reduction. The buyer may choose rejection, acceptance, or partial acceptance.$EXPL$
