-- Q11169: Agency and Regulation [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under the Restatement (Third) of Agency Section 3.07(1), the death of the principal automatically terminates the agent''s authority by operation of law. The lease Shaw signed after Nelson''s death is void and does not bind Nelson''s estate, regardless of Shaw''s lack of knowledge.
Wrong (A): Unlike revocation, which requires notice, termination by death is immediate and does not depend on the agent receiving formal notification.
Wrong (B): The agent''s good faith is irrelevant because the principal''s death extinguishes authority automatically, not upon the agent''s awareness.
Wrong (D): The agency terminates immediately upon death, not merely suspended. Probate proceedings do not affect the timing of termination.$EXPL$
