-- Q11173: Agency and Regulation [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under Section 11 of the Securities Act of 1933, the issuer faces strict liability for material misstatements in the registration statement and cannot assert a due diligence defense. However, other parties including directors, signing officers like the CEO, and underwriters may each assert the defense by proving they conducted a reasonable investigation.
Wrong (A): The CEO may assert due diligence, but the issuer (Pinnacle Energy Corp.) cannot. This choice incorrectly suggests both the CEO and underwriter share the defense without distinguishing the issuer''s strict liability.
Wrong (B): Section 11 imposes strict liability only on the issuer, not on all parties. Non-issuer defendants have affirmative defenses available.
Wrong (D): Corporate officers are legally distinct from the issuer entity and may individually assert the due diligence defense. They do not share the issuer''s strict liability.$EXPL$
