-- Q11178: Agency and Regulation [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under the Restatement (Third) of Agency Section 8.08, an agent owes a duty of care requiring performance with the competence and diligence that a reasonable person would exercise under similar circumstances. This is an objective standard measured against what is reasonable, not perfection.
Wrong (A): The duty of care does not require absolute perfection. An agent who exercises ordinary diligence satisfies the obligation even if the outcome is imperfect.
Wrong (B): The standard requires reasonable competence and diligence, not merely the minimum effort. An agent must act prudently and skillfully.
Wrong (D): The standard is that of a reasonable person in similar circumstances, not the most experienced professional in the field. It is an ordinary care standard, not an expert-level benchmark.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11178;

-- Q11179: Agency and Regulation [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under UCC Article 9, Section 9-322(a)(2), a perfected security interest has priority over an unperfected security interest. Lakeland perfected by filing a UCC-1 financing statement under Section 9-310, while Second National Bank failed to file and remains unperfected.
Wrong (A): Priority under Article 9 is determined by perfection status and filing order, not by which creditor extended credit most recently.
Wrong (B): Secured creditors do not share equally. A perfected interest takes priority over an unperfected interest regardless of the amounts involved.
Wrong (C): Unsecured creditors are subordinate to both perfected and unperfected secured parties under Article 9, not senior to them.$EXPL$
