  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under the Securities Exchange Act of 1934, Section 13(a), publicly traded companies must file periodic reports with the SEC. Form 10-K is the required annual report providing a comprehensive overview of the company''s financial condition and results of operations.
Wrong (B): Form 10-Q is the quarterly report required under the same provision. It is not the annual filing.
Wrong (C): Form 8-K is a current report filed to disclose specific material events (such as mergers or officer changes), not a periodic annual filing.
Wrong (D): Form S-1 is a registration statement under the Securities Act of 1933 used for initial public offerings, not a periodic report under the 1934 Act.$EXPL$
