-- Q11183: Agency and Regulation [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under UCC Section 2-104, a merchant deals in goods of the kind involved in the transaction. UCC Article 2 imposes heightened standards on merchants, including the obligation of good faith and fair dealing consistent with commercial standards of the trade under Section 2-103.
Wrong (A): While implied warranties such as merchantability arise from merchant status under Section 2-314, the UCC does not require a separate written warranty for every item sold.
Wrong (B): The statute of frauds under UCC Section 2-201 applies to contracts for goods priced at $500 or more. Merchant status does not create an exemption from this requirement.
