-- Q11184: Agency and Regulation [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under the Restatement (Third) of Agency Section 3.07(2), the principal''s bankruptcy terminates the agent''s authority by operation of law, effective immediately and without notice. The contract with Omega is void because Hayes had no authority after Gentry''s Chapter 7 filing. Omega may recover damages from Hayes under the implied warranty of authority doctrine.
Wrong (A): Although both Hayes and Omega acted without knowledge, the bankruptcy terminated Hayes''s authority automatically. Good faith does not preserve authority extinguished by operation of law.
Wrong (C): The contract is void, not voidable. Termination by operation of law is absolute; the bankruptcy trustee cannot ratify an act made without any authority.
Wrong (D): A fixed-term agency agreement does not survive the principal''s bankruptcy. Termination by operation of law overrides contractual duration provisions.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11184;

