  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under common law, a CPA owes a duty of care to the client based on the contractual engagement letter. Lakeside can sue Harmon for breach of contract (failure to perform the engagement as agreed) and negligence (failure to exercise reasonable professional care in conducting the audit).
Wrong (B): Section 11 strict liability under the Securities Act of 1933 applies to misstatements in registration statements for public offerings, not to routine audits under private engagement letters.
Wrong (C): Rule 10b-5 requires proof of scienter (intent to deceive) and applies to fraud in connection with securities transactions, not to negligent audit performance.
Wrong (D): A CPA''s duty runs to the audit client under the engagement contract, not as a fiduciary to the client''s shareholders.$EXPL$
