-- Q11186: Agency and Regulation [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under UCC Section 2-305, a contract for the sale of goods can be formed even if the price is left open, provided the parties intended to make a contract. When the price is not settled, the price is a reasonable price at the time of delivery.
Wrong (A): UCC Article 2 departs from common law by allowing open terms, including price, as long as there is intent to contract and a reasonably certain basis for providing a remedy.
Wrong (B): The absence of a price term does not negate contractual intent. The parties'' conduct (ordering, agreeing, and shipping) demonstrates intent to contract.
Wrong (D): Section 2-305 applies to all parties, not only merchants. Both merchant and non-merchant contracts may be enforced with an open price term.$EXPL$
