  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under the Securities Act of 1933, Section 5(b)(1), a preliminary prospectus (informally called a "red herring" because of the red legend on its cover) may be distributed during the waiting period to provide investors with material information about the offering before the final price is set.
Wrong (A): The final prospectus may only be delivered after the registration statement becomes effective, not during the waiting period.
Wrong (B): A tombstone advertisement is a brief public notice of the offering, not the document distributed to gauge investor interest during the waiting period.
